WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.720
(angelic music)

00:00:20.552 --> 00:00:22.690
- Hi! I'm Liz, and I'm from the Midwest,

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.490
where we eat cheese curds.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:25.860
When I moved out to Los Angeles,

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.360
I realized that most people

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.190
have never had these squeaky delights.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.740
So I took to the streets of Hollywood,

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.120
to see if these people
were worth their cheddar.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.151
- Hey what's up, I'm Justin.
- I'm Shaun

00:00:35.151 --> 00:00:36.460
- [both] And we're from South Africa

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.000
- I'm Brian, from
Treasure Island, Florida.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.460
- [man] South Dakota
- [man #2] South Africa

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.920
- [man] Long Island
- [woman] from L.A.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.550
- [woman] Utah!
- [woman #2] Virginia

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.300
- [woman] Napa, California
- [man] I'm from Hollywood

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.680
- [man] Alaska
- [woman] Texas

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.640
- Chicago, Illinois, and I
have never had a cheese curd

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.680
- Let's fondue this.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.180
- [voiceover] What does
it look like to you?

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.730
- [both] Earwax. (laughs)

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.440
- Is this really cheese? I don't know

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.940
- Isn't that like moldy cheese?

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.650
- A soggy cheese puff?

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.610
- Ew, there's... Ew.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:09.602
- Oh my god. (man laughs)
I don't know what that is.

00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:12.370
- That's gnarly. Wow.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:14.250
- But it's delicious.
It's like a cheese fry.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.080
- [girl] Not a huge fan.
- [man] It's really rubbery

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.991
- A cross between Velveeta and Easy Mac.

00:01:20.991 --> 00:01:23.670
Made in a little girl's oven bake.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.590
(sounds of disgust)
[man] I love it!

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.502
- It's rad that it
squeaks when you chew it.

00:01:27.502 --> 00:01:29.720
- [woman] I can't do anymore
- [man] Not bad.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:31.510
- It's like an orgasm in your mouth.

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:33.090
- I'd have them constantly

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.600
- [woman] I thought it wasn't
gonna taste good, honestly.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.640
- [man] Yeah, it' s actually much better

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.190
than I thought it was going to be

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.850
- It's way better than normal cheese.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.770
- Way better than normal cheese?!

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.110
- I would have them again
and again and again and again

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:45.650
and over and over and over.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.070
- I didn't like the texture

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.320
- Can I try one more?

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.910
- [man in black shirt] It's
too rubbery, too chewy.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.240
- [man in white shirt]
Never again, never again.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.830
- It would be great to
get this in South Africa.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.600
- I'd like to make a cheese curd pizza.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.040
Where can I get this?

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.652
- [voiceover] Would you
guys eat this again?

00:01:58.652 --> 00:02:00.130
- [man] I would definitely eat them again

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:02.430
- [man in purple shirt]
Number one, I love it.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.713
- Yeah, right here

00:02:08.713 --> 00:02:10.260
- [man in black shirt] Right here.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.510
- Definitely, I'd give it a ten; top ten.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:14.260
- Can I have some more?

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.680
- Alright guys, here's the cheese curd

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.810
taste test breakdown:
we got alot of these,

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.550
some of these, some of
these, and some of these.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:21.980
People were pretty much
all over the board.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.610
But either way, I think
everyone had a gouda time.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.950
Sorry, that was cheesy. Okay.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:32.160
(upbeat trumpet music)

